1
00:00:18,822 --> 00:00:20,867
Caroline,
open this door and let me in.

2
00:00:21,129 --> 00:00:23,218
You are not taking my baby.

3
00:00:23,305 --> 00:00:24,436
It's a monster.

4
00:00:24,523 --> 00:00:25,959
I will fucking shoot you!

5
00:00:26,221 --> 00:00:28,179
Trust me,
it's what must be done.

6
00:00:28,266 --> 00:00:30,268
You have to give up the baby.

7
00:00:32,705 --> 00:00:33,837
Michael!

8
00:00:37,623 --> 00:00:38,842
I'm coming out.

9
00:00:38,929 --> 00:00:40,974
I will shoot anyone
who comes near me!

10
00:00:53,117 --> 00:00:54,292
Michael!

11
00:01:00,559 --> 00:01:01,647
Michael!

12
00:01:16,706 --> 00:01:19,274
Do you believe now?

13
00:01:36,073 --> 00:01:37,770
How’s it look now?

14
00:01:42,906 --> 00:01:44,342
Yeah,
if we bathed our baby in this,

15
00:01:44,429 --> 00:01:45,952
people will come and take it.

16
00:01:52,220 --> 00:01:54,004
Stella? Try it again.

17
00:01:57,094 --> 00:01:59,227
It's still hell's bathwater.

18
00:01:59,618 --> 00:02:01,229
Oh! Oh no, it's clearing.

19
00:02:03,056 --> 00:02:05,058
Ah!
Look at that.

20
00:02:06,234 --> 00:02:08,366
It almost looks like
water's supposed to.

21
00:02:09,062 --> 00:02:11,152
I think this technically
makes me a plumber.

22
00:02:11,239 --> 00:02:12,501
How many YouTube videos

23
00:02:12,588 --> 00:02:14,198
did you have to watch
to learn that?

24
00:02:14,285 --> 00:02:15,243
Just one.

25
00:02:16,157 --> 00:02:17,419
And five more.

26
00:02:20,857 --> 00:02:22,075
These are great.

27
00:02:22,163 --> 00:02:24,556
I'm not sure
what I wanna do over the crib.

28
00:02:25,122 --> 00:02:26,602
Maybe we can go
into the countryside

29
00:02:26,819 --> 00:02:28,995
when the leaves turn,
get some pictures.

30
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:31,563
Yeah? It's a date.

31
00:02:33,348 --> 00:02:36,525
Speaking of dates, uh,
the shower's a month away,

32
00:02:36,612 --> 00:02:39,310
and you still haven't touched
your stack of invitations.

33
00:02:39,397 --> 00:02:41,921
Construction guys
aren't that into parties

34
00:02:42,008 --> 00:02:43,662
where the food is miniaturized.

35
00:02:44,446 --> 00:02:45,882
Pizza for dinner? I'm starving.

36
00:02:45,969 --> 00:02:49,146
Oh, smooth, smooth deflection.

37
00:02:49,233 --> 00:02:50,626
You said "pizza"
and my whole world

38
00:02:50,713 --> 00:02:52,018
became cheese and pepperoni.

39
00:02:52,105 --> 00:02:53,672
Mm.

40
00:02:56,284 --> 00:02:58,590
I'm not talking
about your work mates,

41
00:02:58,677 --> 00:02:59,635
and you know it.

42
00:03:02,115 --> 00:03:04,466
Your family's about to get
a new member.

43
00:03:06,816 --> 00:03:08,252
If a baby isn't reason enough

44
00:03:08,339 --> 00:03:09,906
to reach out
after all these years--

45
00:03:09,993 --> 00:03:12,778
The last thing
that we want is my family

46
00:03:12,865 --> 00:03:15,041
anywhere near this kid's life.

47
00:03:16,826 --> 00:03:18,741
It's best for everyone,
trust me.

48
00:03:20,221 --> 00:03:22,919
Are you ever gonna tell me
what your issue is with them?

49
00:03:23,006 --> 00:03:24,312
Hey, do you mind
putting the order in,

50
00:03:24,399 --> 00:03:26,096
so it's here when I get back?

51
00:03:27,402 --> 00:03:30,361
What are you in the mood for?
Ah. I don't know. Surprise me.

52
00:03:30,753 --> 00:03:33,059
Oh. Oh.

53
00:03:34,496 --> 00:03:36,454
Someone's doing somersaults.

54
00:03:37,063 --> 00:03:38,630
Come here, feel.

55
00:03:41,546 --> 00:03:42,678
Ian.

56
00:03:48,118 --> 00:03:49,206
Makes it all feel...

57
00:03:50,468 --> 00:03:51,774
very real.

58
00:03:54,255 --> 00:03:55,256
Ian?

59
00:03:56,169 --> 00:03:57,345
Babe, what's wrong?

60
00:03:58,650 --> 00:04:01,610
Nothing. I... I should go.

61
00:04:02,045 --> 00:04:03,960
I need to drop this gear off
before they shut the place.

62
00:04:04,047 --> 00:04:05,875
Let the water run
for another 20 minutes

63
00:04:05,962 --> 00:04:07,398
and then turn it off, okay?

64
00:04:17,669 --> 00:04:19,280
<i>Can you say something?</i>

65
00:04:21,107 --> 00:04:22,457
Are you sure?

66
00:04:23,675 --> 00:04:25,547
I had a vasectomy,
for God's sake.

67
00:04:43,347 --> 00:04:45,610
<i>Ian. Babe, what's wrong?</i>

68
00:04:46,394 --> 00:04:49,266
<i>Are you gonna tell me </i>
<i>what your issue is with them?</i>

69
00:05:33,528 --> 00:05:35,312
Let me help you with that.

70
00:05:38,315 --> 00:05:39,403
Um, thank you.

71
00:05:40,273 --> 00:05:42,188
Sorry, do we--
Know each other?

72
00:05:42,275 --> 00:05:44,626
No, not yet,
but I am hoping to change that.

73
00:05:45,366 --> 00:05:46,541
I'm Caroline Cadell.

74
00:05:48,325 --> 00:05:50,022
Ian's mother.

75
00:05:50,109 --> 00:05:51,807
If now isn't a good time,
I can--

76
00:05:51,894 --> 00:05:55,288
No, no, come in please.

77
00:06:05,211 --> 00:06:06,735
It's a lovely house.

78
00:06:08,998 --> 00:06:10,086
It's got good ...

79
00:06:13,132 --> 00:06:14,395
bones.

80
00:06:15,918 --> 00:06:17,354
We were gonna fix it up.

81
00:06:18,007 --> 00:06:19,922
We were gonna do
a lot of things.

82
00:06:22,011 --> 00:06:24,579
Oh, sorry, can I get you
something to drink?

83
00:06:25,797 --> 00:06:28,974
Uh, yes, a glass of water.
Okay.

84
00:06:29,061 --> 00:06:30,106
In other circumstances,

85
00:06:30,193 --> 00:06:32,108
I'd say we both deserve
a shot of whiskey.

86
00:06:33,762 --> 00:06:35,546
Let's, uh, go outside.

87
00:06:35,633 --> 00:06:38,070
Oh, yeah.
Let me help you with that. Oh, thank you.

88
00:06:38,810 --> 00:06:42,161
Yeah, please, you must sit down.
Your feet must be screaming.

89
00:06:42,248 --> 00:06:45,121
Mine swelled worse with every pregnancy.

90
00:06:51,562 --> 00:06:53,869
You're probably wondering
how I found you.

91
00:06:54,391 --> 00:06:58,047
Imagining some sleazy
private investigator

92
00:06:58,134 --> 00:07:00,789
who's... ...following your every move.

93
00:07:04,793 --> 00:07:05,881
But the truth is...

94
00:07:09,014 --> 00:07:11,234
...we stopped looking for Ian
a long time ago.

95
00:07:13,323 --> 00:07:15,064
Yeah, when he decided to leave.

96
00:07:15,978 --> 00:07:17,458
I can't change it now.

97
00:07:19,372 --> 00:07:21,592
All those arguments
that I practiced in my head,

98
00:07:21,679 --> 00:07:23,333
they're completely useless.

99
00:07:26,858 --> 00:07:28,381
But you are here.

100
00:07:29,513 --> 00:07:31,428
And I would love
to get to know you.

101
00:07:33,604 --> 00:07:35,214
The woman that my son loved.

102
00:07:38,174 --> 00:07:39,392
How did you know that he...

103
00:07:39,567 --> 00:07:43,484
My son-in-law, he stumbled
across the obit online.

104
00:07:45,486 --> 00:07:47,836
Ian, of course, had changed
his last name to Clark.

105
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:50,578
But then there was the photo.

106
00:07:52,493 --> 00:07:53,842
He looked so handsome.

107
00:07:56,061 --> 00:07:57,236
And happy.

108
00:07:58,324 --> 00:08:00,196
I took that photo
on our honeymoon.

109
00:08:02,503 --> 00:08:04,200
I wanted to contact you.

110
00:08:06,245 --> 00:08:08,334
But I never knew
Ian's old last name.

111
00:08:08,857 --> 00:08:10,989
Yes, I'm sure
he hid his past very well.

112
00:08:13,644 --> 00:08:16,255
Was the, um...

113
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:21,217
was the funeral nice?

114
00:08:21,652 --> 00:08:24,350
It was a small service,
just a few friends.

115
00:08:24,437 --> 00:08:25,787
Your family didn't go?

116
00:08:27,353 --> 00:08:29,268
It was just my mom
and I growing up.

117
00:08:30,008 --> 00:08:31,880
Well, she died
when I was in college.

118
00:08:32,837 --> 00:08:34,143
So, you're all alone?

119
00:08:40,062 --> 00:08:41,411
Is it a boy or a girl?

120
00:08:42,194 --> 00:08:43,413
We didn't want to know.

121
00:08:44,719 --> 00:08:46,590
We thought it would be
a nice surprise.

122
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:49,985
Yes, well, babies come
with enough surprises.

123
00:08:54,598 --> 00:08:55,599
Stella...

124
00:08:57,993 --> 00:09:00,952
my children are all coming to
the summer cottage this weekend.

125
00:09:02,867 --> 00:09:04,129
And I would love it...

126
00:09:06,871 --> 00:09:08,220
if you would join us.

127
00:09:09,004 --> 00:09:11,920
If it's a family thing,
I... I...

128
00:09:13,138 --> 00:09:15,314
You have the last piece
of my son inside you.

129
00:09:18,448 --> 00:09:19,710
That makes you family.

130
00:09:21,451 --> 00:09:22,626
Please.

131
00:10:20,553 --> 00:10:23,382
Cottage? If you say so.

132
00:10:36,265 --> 00:10:37,396
Whoa, okay.

133
00:10:59,462 --> 00:11:02,770
Oh. Do you want me
to pee in your bushes?

134
00:11:11,474 --> 00:11:13,781
Hello.

135
00:11:24,661 --> 00:11:26,054
Hello. Anyone home?

136
00:11:27,577 --> 00:11:28,578
I can't believe

137
00:11:28,665 --> 00:11:30,319
we're having
this conversation again.

138
00:11:30,406 --> 00:11:31,624
What do you mean again?

139
00:11:31,799 --> 00:11:34,366
What do I mean?
Fifty grand, down the drain!

140
00:11:34,453 --> 00:11:37,108
We agreed
I can spend as I see fit.

141
00:11:37,195 --> 00:11:38,631
You know,
spending and squandering

142
00:11:38,719 --> 00:11:41,417
are not the same thing!
It's my money, Lake.

143
00:11:41,504 --> 00:11:43,985
Your allowance, you mean.
We agreed not to use that word.

144
00:11:44,072 --> 00:11:46,422
You agreed not to use it.
Look, you don't know,

145
00:11:46,509 --> 00:11:49,599
the investment
might still pay off. Like all your other investments?

146
00:11:49,686 --> 00:11:51,079
If you really wanna use booze

147
00:11:51,166 --> 00:11:52,558
as an excuse
for being a bitch, sweetie,

148
00:11:52,645 --> 00:11:54,125
you should really try
and drink it first.

149
00:11:54,212 --> 00:11:55,779
Or maybe I should
just dump it on the floor.

150
00:11:55,866 --> 00:11:57,259
I mean, that's
what gets you off, isn't it?

151
00:11:57,346 --> 00:11:58,608
Wasting my money.

152
00:11:58,695 --> 00:12:00,653
Oh, what's this,
about 20 quid's worth?

153
00:12:00,741 --> 00:12:03,178
Shall I make it a double, hmm?

154
00:12:03,874 --> 00:12:05,876
Sorry. I'm... I'm so sorry.

155
00:12:05,963 --> 00:12:07,748
I... I did knock,
but no one answered,

156
00:12:07,835 --> 00:12:10,489
and I...
I really need the bathroom.

157
00:12:11,708 --> 00:12:14,929
I'm Stella.
Yeah, yeah, we know. We all Googled you.

158
00:12:15,016 --> 00:12:16,017
Nice LinkedIn pic.

159
00:12:16,321 --> 00:12:19,107
So, you do know
what a job site is? Chew glass.

160
00:12:19,194 --> 00:12:22,110
How about I pour this on my feet
and you lap it up like a puppy?

161
00:12:22,197 --> 00:12:25,417
Oh, please don't get
any whiskey on the oriental.

162
00:12:26,418 --> 00:12:29,334
You can still say that
about rugs, I hope. Hello.

163
00:12:30,379 --> 00:12:33,121
Save the casual racism
for dinner, shall we, Mother?

164
00:12:33,469 --> 00:12:34,905
She has to pee.

165
00:12:35,471 --> 00:12:36,907
Yeah.

166
00:12:37,081 --> 00:12:39,736
Curse of pregnancy. Yes, one of them.

167
00:12:39,823 --> 00:12:41,738
It's just down the hall
on the left.

168
00:12:42,130 --> 00:12:43,044
Okay.

169
00:12:47,222 --> 00:12:48,484
Are you serious?

170
00:12:48,571 --> 00:12:49,964
What?
Keep it together.

171
00:12:57,972 --> 00:12:59,060
Oh.

172
00:13:00,931 --> 00:13:03,064
The water was smooth as silk.

173
00:13:03,629 --> 00:13:05,849
Weatherman said
it was gonna be scorching today.

174
00:13:05,936 --> 00:13:08,330
Shows what they know.
You must be freezing.

175
00:13:08,417 --> 00:13:12,508
Cold is good for the soul,
and you can withstand anything

176
00:13:12,595 --> 00:13:14,249
if you put your mind to it.

177
00:13:14,945 --> 00:13:17,295
I used to tell Ian that

178
00:13:17,556 --> 00:13:20,037
when he had the
night terrors as a boy.

179
00:13:20,821 --> 00:13:22,518
Did he ever grow out of them?

180
00:13:22,605 --> 00:13:24,085
Perhaps, you...

181
00:13:25,347 --> 00:13:27,784
perhaps, you should go
and get ready for dinner.

182
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:30,482
You're worried she'll run,

183
00:13:31,005 --> 00:13:35,270
screaming at the sight
of my nylon-clad bosom.

184
00:13:35,618 --> 00:13:37,620
She looks tougher than that.

185
00:13:41,058 --> 00:13:44,279
She's a bit of
a character, Grandma Odette.

186
00:13:44,366 --> 00:13:47,978
The children call her Granno.
Your mother?

187
00:13:49,850 --> 00:13:51,025
My late husband's.

188
00:13:52,504 --> 00:13:53,723
Come with me.

189
00:14:04,386 --> 00:14:08,085
I've put you in Ian's old room.

190
00:14:14,483 --> 00:14:16,877
It's a bit further
away than the others,

191
00:14:17,138 --> 00:14:20,315
but I thought you might
like that, the privacy.

192
00:14:21,359 --> 00:14:23,057
Oh, and it has an en suite.

193
00:14:24,058 --> 00:14:26,451
I should get you
some fresh towels.

194
00:14:26,974 --> 00:14:28,627
It's the help's week off.

195
00:14:31,369 --> 00:14:33,763
Most of his things
have been put away in boxes now.

196
00:14:35,286 --> 00:14:38,159
Rugby trophies... ...those awful band posters,

197
00:14:38,333 --> 00:14:39,595
video games.

198
00:14:40,074 --> 00:14:43,164
Other things that I just
couldn't bear to put away.

199
00:14:53,174 --> 00:14:54,871
No matter
what he told you, Stella.

200
00:14:56,873 --> 00:14:58,048
It wasn't all bad.

201
00:15:00,050 --> 00:15:01,443
It's happy memories.

202
00:15:01,965 --> 00:15:03,010
Good times.

203
00:15:03,793 --> 00:15:05,273
Families are complicated.

204
00:15:08,537 --> 00:15:09,712
Dinner's at 7:00.

205
00:15:27,425 --> 00:15:29,079
How's that drink, Granno?

206
00:15:29,166 --> 00:15:30,733
Mm. It's nice.

207
00:15:30,820 --> 00:15:32,517
I don't usually
like things with lemon,

208
00:15:32,604 --> 00:15:34,215
but this is okay.

209
00:15:36,478 --> 00:15:38,741
Has anybody heard from him?

210
00:15:38,828 --> 00:15:41,178
I mean we've got time,
but we've just gotta make sure

211
00:15:41,265 --> 00:15:43,180
that Stella
doesn't get suspicious.

212
00:15:43,267 --> 00:15:45,008
I hope
things stay on schedule.

213
00:15:45,095 --> 00:15:47,358
I really can't be away
from the firm forever.

214
00:15:47,445 --> 00:15:50,144
You work too much.
It's affecting your complexion.

215
00:15:50,231 --> 00:15:51,667
Thanks, Granno.

216
00:15:51,841 --> 00:15:53,669
Felix takes enough time off
for the both of us,

217
00:15:53,756 --> 00:15:55,932
don't you, darling?
Did you want bitters in your tonic,

218
00:15:56,019 --> 00:15:57,847
or do you just produce
them naturally?

219
00:15:57,934 --> 00:15:59,501
Felix!

220
00:16:00,371 --> 00:16:04,636
Cadell babies come early,
and she does look close.

221
00:16:04,723 --> 00:16:05,898
I wouldn't worry.

222
00:16:05,986 --> 00:16:08,379
Ian always did go
for the Pollyannas.

223
00:16:08,466 --> 00:16:11,817
Ho, ho, ho, ho, ho.
Merry Christmas!

224
00:16:11,904 --> 00:16:13,645
It's summer, darling.

225
00:16:13,732 --> 00:16:16,039
Well, Santa spent
the Lord's b-day

226
00:16:16,126 --> 00:16:19,477
with a raging hangover,
but he's here now.

227
00:16:19,564 --> 00:16:23,438
Sister of mine, present for thee.

228
00:16:27,746 --> 00:16:29,400
Is this new or did you
try it out for me?

229
00:16:29,487 --> 00:16:31,924
Oh, aren't you hysterical?
Mwah, mwah.

230
00:16:32,447 --> 00:16:34,275
And what
have we got for Felix?

231
00:16:34,405 --> 00:16:36,146
It's an old bottle of scotch.

232
00:16:36,233 --> 00:16:39,019
Half empty, but you're used
to living off Lake's scraps, eh?

233
00:16:40,542 --> 00:16:43,371
Oh, it's so good
to have our Benjamin Bunny back.

234
00:16:43,458 --> 00:16:44,981
No, stop.

235
00:16:45,068 --> 00:16:47,201
And last but not least.

236
00:16:47,288 --> 00:16:49,551
Oh, what to get
for the delicate flower

237
00:16:49,638 --> 00:16:51,814
who ejected me from her loins?

238
00:16:52,510 --> 00:16:54,643
Hmm.
Oh, thank you.

239
00:16:54,730 --> 00:16:57,037
Finally, something to beat
some common sense

240
00:16:57,124 --> 00:16:58,603
into the lot of you.

241
00:16:58,690 --> 00:16:59,996
So,
where's the baby mama?

242
00:17:00,910 --> 00:17:02,651
I... I'm here.

243
00:17:03,260 --> 00:17:07,221
You? You're my brother's
pregnant widow.

244
00:17:08,439 --> 00:17:11,660
Huh. I'm afraid
Santa forgot your gift.

245
00:17:11,747 --> 00:17:12,791
It's okay.

246
00:17:13,662 --> 00:17:14,706
Hang on.

247
00:17:18,971 --> 00:17:21,713
Ian gave it to me
when I passed my A levels.

248
00:17:22,584 --> 00:17:23,846
Take it, I insist.

249
00:17:28,677 --> 00:17:29,852
Thank you.

250
00:17:30,374 --> 00:17:32,376
Well, who wants sea bass?

251
00:17:32,463 --> 00:17:34,030
Oh, me. Me, me, please.
Yes.

252
00:17:34,117 --> 00:17:36,380
I am starving.

253
00:17:36,467 --> 00:17:40,950
20K. 20K,
and in three weeks, four weeks.

254
00:17:58,794 --> 00:18:00,796
So, where are you from, Stella?

255
00:18:00,926 --> 00:18:02,928
I grew up in Ilford, in Essex.

256
00:18:03,015 --> 00:18:03,886
Oh, dear.

257
00:18:03,973 --> 00:18:06,367
More chocolate silk pie, dear?

258
00:18:06,454 --> 00:18:09,196
No, thank you.
I couldn't eat another bite, um.

259
00:18:09,892 --> 00:18:12,242
I should
probably call it a night.

260
00:18:12,329 --> 00:18:14,070
Uh, it's been
a really long day and,

261
00:18:14,592 --> 00:18:17,204
well, I shot
a fifth birthday party

262
00:18:17,291 --> 00:18:19,989
at a Gymboree,
just to make some extra cash.

263
00:18:20,685 --> 00:18:24,733
I have about 100 photos to edit.
What the fuck's a Gymboree?

264
00:18:24,820 --> 00:18:26,561
I've got a confession
to make, Stella.

265
00:18:27,475 --> 00:18:31,218
I saw you earlier
listening out in the hallway.

266
00:18:31,305 --> 00:18:34,960
So, I know that you know
that we're hiding something.

267
00:18:36,788 --> 00:18:38,181
I wasn't--
Relax.

268
00:18:40,270 --> 00:18:43,186
It's not as if a baby shower
is the secret of the century.

269
00:18:47,277 --> 00:18:49,279
Oh, you...

270
00:18:49,366 --> 00:18:51,063
Wow, you don't...
you don't have to do that.

271
00:18:51,151 --> 00:18:53,805
Oh, no, we must celebrate you
and the little one.

272
00:18:53,892 --> 00:18:55,633
It's just going to be
a family affair.

273
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:57,113
Very quiet. Low-key.

274
00:19:10,692 --> 00:19:12,128
Champagne is meant
to served immediately!

275
00:19:12,215 --> 00:19:13,999
This is fucking warm! Go fix it.

276
00:19:14,086 --> 00:19:15,827
I was just telling Derek,

277
00:19:15,914 --> 00:19:18,003
it's great having an excuse
for us all to get together.

278
00:19:18,134 --> 00:19:20,267
<i>Are you planning</i>
<i>on eating the placenta?</i>

279
00:19:20,354 --> 00:19:23,052
You look lovely.
Absolutely glowing.

280
00:19:23,139 --> 00:19:26,229
<i>Don’t be afraid of labor. </i>
<i>That’s the easy part.</i>

281
00:19:26,316 --> 00:19:28,275
<i>It’s raising them that's hard.</i>

282
00:19:28,362 --> 00:19:31,452
Think happy thoughts.

283
00:19:43,420 --> 00:19:45,553
Do you mind pouring me
one of those?

284
00:19:46,380 --> 00:19:48,077
Sure.

285
00:19:48,295 --> 00:19:49,948
They threw me one last month.

286
00:19:50,645 --> 00:19:52,124
Felt like someone ran me over,

287
00:19:52,212 --> 00:19:54,257
and then dropped presents
on top of my body.

288
00:19:55,171 --> 00:19:57,129
Yeah.

289
00:19:57,217 --> 00:19:59,480
I'm Rose. Henry's wife.

290
00:20:00,132 --> 00:20:03,788
He and Ian were cousins.
Twice removed or something.

291
00:20:05,268 --> 00:20:06,878
My condolences, by the way.

292
00:20:07,183 --> 00:20:09,229
I can't imagine going
through this alone.

293
00:20:10,230 --> 00:20:13,929
Listen, when they tell
you anything about-- Rose, come here.

294
00:20:15,365 --> 00:20:19,239
I'm being summoned.
Um, maybe we will talk again?

295
00:20:20,370 --> 00:20:22,720
Oh, and don't worry
about the insect.

296
00:20:23,243 --> 00:20:25,375
It doesn't bite or anything.
Rose.

297
00:20:26,942 --> 00:20:27,986
Coming, darling.

298
00:20:29,161 --> 00:20:31,294
Insect? What?

299
00:20:55,579 --> 00:20:57,755
No offense, but...

300
00:20:58,669 --> 00:21:01,106
you're going to be too heavy
for me to carry inside

301
00:21:01,193 --> 00:21:02,673
if you do decide
to go into labor.

302
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:05,197
Uh, this one's got me running
about a million degrees,

303
00:21:05,285 --> 00:21:07,330
so the cold water feels nice.

304
00:21:07,591 --> 00:21:09,811
So I'm not the only one
that needed a breather.

305
00:21:13,902 --> 00:21:15,904
I can't believe
how many people came.

306
00:21:16,992 --> 00:21:19,124
They don't even know me.
Our family's a little weird,

307
00:21:19,211 --> 00:21:21,213
but you might have
sussed that already.

308
00:21:22,389 --> 00:21:23,738
But they mean well.

309
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:27,437
Come on.

310
00:21:28,438 --> 00:21:30,005
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.
Please?

311
00:21:30,092 --> 00:21:31,223
No. Okay.

312
00:21:32,573 --> 00:21:34,357
Let me get my glasses.
One second.

313
00:21:37,665 --> 00:21:38,927
Nice. One more?

314
00:21:39,928 --> 00:21:41,364
Yes.

315
00:21:41,451 --> 00:21:42,757
I think this is
my better side anyway.

316
00:21:44,498 --> 00:21:46,717
You want a pound's worth
of free advice?

317
00:21:47,065 --> 00:21:48,719
Thought the going rate
was a penny.

318
00:21:49,372 --> 00:21:50,895
Yeah, well, mine's worth more.

319
00:21:53,855 --> 00:21:55,422
Whatever's going to happen...

320
00:21:57,075 --> 00:21:58,076
let it.

321
00:21:58,773 --> 00:22:00,644
Fighting just makes it worse.

322
00:22:03,212 --> 00:22:04,518
Oh, case in point.

323
00:22:05,867 --> 00:22:06,998
It's time.

324
00:22:07,782 --> 00:22:08,913
Come on in.

325
00:22:10,001 --> 00:22:13,091
This tradition has been
in the family for generations.

326
00:22:13,178 --> 00:22:16,007
Granno's done it, I've done it,
and now, it's your turn.

327
00:22:16,617 --> 00:22:18,880
Just now, lie down here.

328
00:22:20,011 --> 00:22:21,056
Really?
Mm.

329
00:22:22,971 --> 00:22:26,191
It's nothing to be scared of.
It's just a little insect

330
00:22:26,278 --> 00:22:27,889
that we're going to drop
on your belly,

331
00:22:27,976 --> 00:22:30,457
and it'll land
on its back or its feet.

332
00:22:30,544 --> 00:22:33,024
So, one way means a boy,
the other means a girl.

333
00:22:33,373 --> 00:22:35,810
Which is which?
Hello!

334
00:22:45,080 --> 00:22:49,998
Are you ready?

335
00:23:09,409 --> 00:23:11,628
Oh, I just wish
I could convince you

336
00:23:11,715 --> 00:23:12,977
to stay with us longer.

337
00:23:13,064 --> 00:23:16,416
I have to get back tomorrow.
I'm so behind with work.

338
00:23:16,981 --> 00:23:18,069
Of course.

339
00:23:18,505 --> 00:23:20,071
But I'll visit
when the baby comes.

340
00:23:21,029 --> 00:23:22,117
How about a nightcap?

341
00:23:22,770 --> 00:23:25,990
A virgin one
for the mama-to-be, naturally.

342
00:23:27,992 --> 00:23:32,257
I hope you felt showered
by Cadell love today.

343
00:23:35,347 --> 00:23:37,306
Granno.
Thank you.

344
00:23:40,614 --> 00:23:43,399
May this baby
be everything that we hope,

345
00:23:43,486 --> 00:23:45,836
nothing more,
nothing less. Cheers.

346
00:23:45,923 --> 00:23:46,794
Cheers.
Cheers.

347
00:23:46,881 --> 00:23:48,056
Cheers.
Cheers.

348
00:23:56,412 --> 00:23:58,066
Thank you, darling.
My pleasure.

349
00:23:59,284 --> 00:24:00,895
You've all been so generous.

350
00:24:00,982 --> 00:24:04,072
I could never have afforded
most of those things on my own,

351
00:24:04,159 --> 00:24:06,204
so thank you.

352
00:24:06,814 --> 00:24:08,903
Well, if that's your way
of asking if we're going to fund

353
00:24:08,990 --> 00:24:11,253
the baby going
forward, then...

354
00:24:11,340 --> 00:24:14,474
No, I would never ex--
Oh darling, I'm just teasing.

355
00:24:15,213 --> 00:24:18,347
Though you probably should.
And we are happy to help.

356
00:24:18,913 --> 00:24:21,132
It's not always easy marrying
into the Cadell family,

357
00:24:21,219 --> 00:24:24,614
but trust me,
we take care of our own.

358
00:24:26,747 --> 00:24:27,878
That's very kind.

359
00:24:30,446 --> 00:24:31,708
Okay.

360
00:24:36,757 --> 00:24:38,628
I think I stood up
too quickly.

361
00:24:38,715 --> 00:24:41,675
Uh, thank you
again for everything.

362
00:24:46,767 --> 00:24:47,811
Good night, everyone.

363
00:24:50,597 --> 00:24:51,685
Good luck.

364
00:24:52,642 --> 00:24:53,556
You too.

365
00:24:59,301 --> 00:25:02,478
Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay.

366
00:25:04,349 --> 00:25:06,482
Hey. It’s okay.
I need some help here!

367
00:25:07,439 --> 00:25:09,050
You have Ian's nose.

368
00:25:12,967 --> 00:25:14,359
<i>Pre-eclampsia.</i>

369
00:25:14,838 --> 00:25:16,927
Your pressure's off the charts.

370
00:25:17,014 --> 00:25:19,060
Couple that
with the loss of balance.

371
00:25:19,147 --> 00:25:21,236
What does that mean?
Is the baby--

372
00:25:21,323 --> 00:25:23,020
Oh, completely fine.

373
00:25:23,891 --> 00:25:26,676
I... I should probably
go to a hospital.

374
00:25:26,763 --> 00:25:29,461
Well, all they'd do
is run the same tests I did.

375
00:25:30,071 --> 00:25:32,726
I mean, the best prescription
for pre-eclampsia

376
00:25:32,813 --> 00:25:36,294
is complete rest.

377
00:25:36,599 --> 00:25:39,515
Luckily, you only have
a short time till you deliver.

378
00:25:39,602 --> 00:25:42,605
Derek is the top OB-GYN
in the country.

379
00:25:43,867 --> 00:25:46,087
You can get up
to go to the bathroom,

380
00:25:46,174 --> 00:25:49,307
uh, shower once a day,
walk a little.

381
00:25:49,873 --> 00:25:52,441
Apart from that,
you take it easy.

382
00:25:52,833 --> 00:25:56,619
No cooking, no cleaning,
no strenuous exercise.

383
00:25:56,924 --> 00:25:58,621
Well, I... I live alone.

384
00:25:58,795 --> 00:26:01,493
Well, the last thing
we want to see is for you

385
00:26:01,581 --> 00:26:04,627
to have a similar episode
on a long drive.

386
00:26:05,541 --> 00:26:07,108
It could be fatal.

387
00:26:07,499 --> 00:26:09,414
We could take care of her here.

388
00:26:09,501 --> 00:26:11,634
I... I can't ask you to do that.

389
00:26:11,721 --> 00:26:14,463
Oh, Stella,
I know that you wanna be home

390
00:26:14,550 --> 00:26:15,595
where things are familiar,

391
00:26:15,943 --> 00:26:17,945
but we've got to listen
to Derek.

392
00:26:18,206 --> 00:26:20,338
We can be your home,
your family.

393
00:26:22,732 --> 00:26:23,820
This is the last thing

394
00:26:23,907 --> 00:26:25,605
that I will ever get to do
for my son.

395
00:26:28,259 --> 00:26:29,521
Please, will you stay?

396
00:26:37,094 --> 00:26:39,183
Okay.

397
00:27:06,689 --> 00:27:07,690
Stella.

398
00:27:08,735 --> 00:27:09,823
Stella.

399
00:27:10,693 --> 00:27:13,174
Oh! There you are.

400
00:27:13,261 --> 00:27:15,959
Oh, Derek said it was okay to...
Yes, no, of course.

401
00:27:16,438 --> 00:27:20,311
Um, I was just wondering
if you felt like going out,

402
00:27:20,398 --> 00:27:22,444
taking a walk,
getting some fresh air?

403
00:27:22,923 --> 00:27:24,881
Mm. Okay.

404
00:27:24,968 --> 00:27:25,839
Great.

405
00:27:26,753 --> 00:27:28,493
I'll finish. Yes.

406
00:27:30,931 --> 00:27:32,584
So,
you've got your phone,

407
00:27:32,672 --> 00:27:34,761
you've got your laptop,
extra pillows.

408
00:27:34,848 --> 00:27:36,980
Is there anything else
I can get for you?

409
00:27:38,025 --> 00:27:39,896
Can you get this baby
out of me faster?

410
00:27:39,983 --> 00:27:42,203
No. No, no, you must never wish for that.

411
00:27:42,725 --> 00:27:44,335
I mean, what if something were
to go wrong,

412
00:27:44,422 --> 00:27:46,337
and then this would be
the only time

413
00:27:46,424 --> 00:27:49,123
that you had with her?
It'd be irreplaceable.

414
00:27:50,428 --> 00:27:51,560
Her?

415
00:27:53,997 --> 00:27:54,998
Oh.

416
00:27:56,086 --> 00:27:57,740
I don't suppose that, um...

417
00:27:58,654 --> 00:28:01,048
Ian told you that I lost a baby.

418
00:28:05,530 --> 00:28:07,315
I-- After Bunny.

419
00:28:08,316 --> 00:28:10,753
She was, um, she was stillborn

420
00:28:10,840 --> 00:28:12,537
and the only time
I got to spend with her

421
00:28:12,624 --> 00:28:14,235
was when she was inside me.

422
00:28:15,540 --> 00:28:17,281
Caroline, I’m so sorry.

423
00:28:17,847 --> 00:28:19,240
It was a long time ago.

424
00:28:22,547 --> 00:28:25,159
But you guys really didn't need
to go to all this trouble.

425
00:28:26,290 --> 00:28:27,770
It's what families do.

426
00:28:28,379 --> 00:28:31,295
Mm. My mom
was more of a "get drunk

427
00:28:31,382 --> 00:28:35,778
and miss my dance recital" type.
Oh, no.

428
00:28:35,865 --> 00:28:37,998
Well, you know what they say,
you can't pick your family,

429
00:28:38,085 --> 00:28:40,000
but you can pick your in-laws.

430
00:28:41,044 --> 00:28:42,829
Usually.

431
00:28:42,916 --> 00:28:47,311
And you, my dear, have...
very overprotective ones.

432
00:28:49,357 --> 00:28:50,401
Sit, darling.

433
00:28:52,447 --> 00:28:53,753
Can I ask you a question?

434
00:28:54,101 --> 00:28:55,015
Mm?

435
00:28:58,627 --> 00:29:00,107
Why did Ian leave home?

436
00:29:01,848 --> 00:29:03,284
He was in love.

437
00:29:05,460 --> 00:29:08,202
She was wrong for the family,
and everyone could see that.

438
00:29:08,680 --> 00:29:10,421
I'm not sure I understand.

439
00:29:11,945 --> 00:29:13,947
The Cadells
are a very old family.

440
00:29:14,948 --> 00:29:17,428
Some people might say
that we're set in our ways.

441
00:29:18,342 --> 00:29:20,170
There definitely are
one or two requirements

442
00:29:20,257 --> 00:29:21,171
that need to be met.

443
00:29:23,173 --> 00:29:24,348
It's about character.

444
00:29:25,349 --> 00:29:26,873
And to be a part of this family,

445
00:29:27,482 --> 00:29:28,439
you might be...

446
00:29:29,832 --> 00:29:32,095
called upon
to meet one or two...

447
00:29:34,054 --> 00:29:35,316
obligations.

448
00:29:36,970 --> 00:29:38,362
Ian struggled with that.

449
00:29:41,104 --> 00:29:44,281
And if Ian had...
brought me home.

450
00:29:49,852 --> 00:29:51,898
If Ian had brought you home...

451
00:29:53,029 --> 00:29:54,944
I'd have said...

452
00:29:55,945 --> 00:29:57,294
that he brought someone home

453
00:29:57,381 --> 00:29:59,949
who was strong enough
to do what needed to be done.

454
00:30:30,284 --> 00:30:31,763
Hello.

455
00:30:31,938 --> 00:30:33,722
<i>Hi, this is Rebecca</i>

456
00:30:33,809 --> 00:30:35,811
<i>from Dr. Wilkinson's office.</i>

457
00:30:36,116 --> 00:30:37,813
<i>Your mother-in-law</i>
<i>called earlier,</i>

458
00:30:37,900 --> 00:30:39,554
<i>and she wanted me</i>
<i>to let you know</i>

459
00:30:39,641 --> 00:30:41,512
<i>she spoke with Dr. Cadell.</i>

460
00:30:42,078 --> 00:30:44,167
Uh, does Dr. Wilkinson
wanna see me?

461
00:30:44,298 --> 00:30:46,953
<i>Oh, no need. </i>
<i>She concurs with Dr. Cadell</i>

462
00:30:47,040 --> 00:30:49,433
<i>that bed rest </i>
<i>is the right course,</i>

463
00:30:49,520 --> 00:30:51,653
and recommends
you have your baby there.

464
00:30:52,219 --> 00:30:54,221
If that's what's best
for the baby.

465
00:30:54,308 --> 00:30:56,310
<i>Mm-hmm. </i>
<i>Have a nice day, my lover.</i>

466
00:30:56,397 --> 00:30:57,354
Bye.

467
00:31:01,663 --> 00:31:03,795
You must be starved.

468
00:31:03,883 --> 00:31:05,710
Pretty much always.

469
00:31:08,191 --> 00:31:09,105
There.

470
00:31:11,281 --> 00:31:13,980
Oh, is that garlic?

471
00:31:14,067 --> 00:31:15,633
Nature's purifier.

472
00:31:15,720 --> 00:31:18,201
Keeps toxins
and other nasties out.

473
00:31:18,288 --> 00:31:21,117
It quite potent.

474
00:31:21,204 --> 00:31:22,902
I think I'll just
stick with toast.

475
00:31:22,989 --> 00:31:24,686
You need protein, dear.

476
00:31:24,773 --> 00:31:27,863
And garlic helps
lower blood pressure.

477
00:31:27,950 --> 00:31:31,780
We want mommy
and baby healthy, don't we?

478
00:31:35,044 --> 00:31:35,958
Okay.

479
00:31:40,397 --> 00:31:43,966
Little stuffy in here. No.

480
00:31:45,011 --> 00:31:45,925
Ah.

481
00:31:46,577 --> 00:31:47,578
Now.

482
00:31:51,713 --> 00:31:52,844
What are those?

483
00:31:52,932 --> 00:31:54,542
Lucky charms.

484
00:31:54,629 --> 00:31:57,110
Ian's grandfather,
my late husband,

485
00:31:57,197 --> 00:31:58,981
brought them back from Sudan.

486
00:31:59,764 --> 00:32:02,854
Gave them to me
on our first anniversary.

487
00:32:07,555 --> 00:32:08,904
Now then.

488
00:32:12,647 --> 00:32:13,778
Ta-da.

489
00:32:14,779 --> 00:32:16,259
Get up, get up.

490
00:32:17,217 --> 00:32:19,175
Is that for me?

491
00:32:19,262 --> 00:32:21,177
Shall we see if it fits?

492
00:32:22,613 --> 00:32:25,703
I'm... I'm fine, thank you.
Arms up.

493
00:32:26,661 --> 00:32:28,445
There. Off.

494
00:32:30,186 --> 00:32:33,363
This way round.

495
00:32:33,450 --> 00:32:35,235
And...

496
00:32:36,540 --> 00:32:37,672
there.

497
00:32:38,847 --> 00:32:40,849
Oh, you look lovely.

498
00:32:41,763 --> 00:32:43,417
I wore that gown

499
00:32:44,287 --> 00:32:46,898
for the last weeks
of both my pregnancies,

500
00:32:46,986 --> 00:32:52,252
and both my babies
were healthy and beautiful.

501
00:32:53,122 --> 00:32:55,124
It's nice and cool, isn't it?

502
00:33:17,755 --> 00:33:18,974
What are you doing in here?

503
00:33:19,279 --> 00:33:22,978
Sorry, I know one of these
is loose as a whore's drawers.

504
00:33:24,501 --> 00:33:26,155
Ah, there it is. Yes.

505
00:33:29,158 --> 00:33:31,639
Do cigarettes go bad,
or are they like Twiglets?

506
00:33:31,726 --> 00:33:33,162
It's the middle
of the night, Bunny.

507
00:33:33,858 --> 00:33:35,208
I couldn't sleep.

508
00:33:36,078 --> 00:33:37,036
I get lonely.

509
00:33:37,993 --> 00:33:40,213
You know, it's a shame

510
00:33:40,300 --> 00:33:42,693
you can't order people
like you can pizzas.

511
00:33:43,390 --> 00:33:45,218
Yeah, Domino's, hi.
Yeah, it's Bunny.

512
00:33:45,305 --> 00:33:48,569
I would like to order
a rugged brunette,

513
00:33:48,873 --> 00:33:50,310
six feet, eight inches.

514
00:33:51,006 --> 00:33:53,182
